 34S  dE EAV,LOGFT$From BetaShape v2.4 (Jun-2024) 2023Mo21.                     
 34S  c  {+34}Cl ground state EC and |b{++} decay.                              
 34S  c  1980Wi13: {+34}Clm was produced via the {+31}P(|a,n) reaction with 10  
 34S 2c  and 11-MeV |a beams from the ONR-CIT tandem accelerator impinging on   
 34S 3c  MnP powder pressed in Be, Zr, and Al forils. |g rays were detected     
 34S 4c  using a 100-cm{+3} Ge(Li) detector. Measured E|g, I|g. Deduced 34S     
 34S 5c  levels, T{-1/2}, decay branching ratios, and log {Ift} for             
 34S 6c  {+34}Cl{+m}|)34S decay. Also measured {+34}Cl ground-state decay.      
 34S  c  1975Va02: {+34}Cl{+m} was produced via the {+24}Mg({+12}C,pn) reaction 
 34S 2c  with a 35-MeV {+12}C beam from the Utrecht EN tandem accelerator. After
 34S 3c  one hour of bombardment, the radioactivity was detected using a        
 34S 4c  100-cm{+2} Ge(Li) detector and a 23|*28-cm{+2} NaI(Tl) detector for    
 34S 5c  Compton suppression. Measured E|g, I|g. Deduced 34S levels, T{-1/2},   
 34S 6c  decay branching ratios, and log {Ift} for {+34}Cl{+m}|)34S decay. Also 
 34S 7c  measured {+34}Cl ground-state decay.                                   
 34S  c  1983Kr06: {+34}Cl{+m} was produced via the {+35}Cl(p,pn) reaction with 
 34S 2c  25-MeV protons from the isochronous cyclotron of the Karlsruhe Research
 34S 3c  Center impinging on a NaCl target on a thin gold backing. The reaction 
 34S 4c  products were separated using a magnetic spectrometer and detected in  
 34S 5c  its focal plane by a Si(Li) detector. Measured E|b using the iron-free 
 34S 6c  magnetic double-lens spectrometer. Deduced end-point energies, |b      
 34S 7c  branching ratios, and Fermi and Gamow-Teller shape factors.            
 34S  c  Half-life measurements: 2006Ia05, 1983Ko22, 1976Wi08, 1973Ry01,        
 34S 2c  1972Ha82, 1965Eb01, 1965Fr06, 1961Ja22, 1960Ja12, 1958Mi85, 1954Kl36   
 34S  c  |b{++} spectrum measurement: 1956Gr07, 1953St42, 1951Ru24              
 34S  d  |b polarization measurement: M. Deutsch et al., Phys. Rev. 107, 1733   
 34S 2d  (1957).                                                                
